Z||000003||tgowens||11-18-2001||09:51 PM||||ok....... go to the bottom of this page and download the Pennock's Image Poster to your machine..... open the program and follow the directions - you will be posting photos in no time!!<P>As for the body alignment -- still a little vague here....... the upper clip mounts to the frame with 10mm bolts on the top and rear (behind the fascia) - the fascia mnounts to the body with large plastic pop-rivits (appx 7 on top and 7 underneath the car and also mounts to the rear quarter panels and rear wheel liners with 7mm screws......there is a metal plate which the fascia fastens to on the top which is bolted to the rear of the frame with 13mm bolts. The rear shock absorbing material (under the fascia) bolts to the frame with two 15mm bolts and two large plastic pop-rivits -- all of this is off of the top of my head so I may have missed someting but that is mostly it........<P>Other than that, I'm not sure what you are asking.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
